SWR-006 — INTEGRATION BE (backend-lead) + CODE_REVIEW round 1 fixes (F-1, F-2, F-5, F-8)
Date: 2026-11-19. Machine: macOS (darwin), local. QA may have been running Playwright in parallel; no e2e / verify run here (frontend-lead runs the final gate).
apps/api/.env was never read or printed. No real OpenAI call (test config: OPENAI_ENABLED=false, AI_COMMANDER_PROVIDER=bot except fake strategies).

== Fixes ==
F-1  apps/api/src/sessions/automation/settle-run.ts (NEW: settleRun + bestEffortEnvelope, shared non-throwing guard);
     sessions.service.ts create path uses settleRun + bestEffortEnvelope; session-commands.service.ts safeRun delegates to settleRun.
     Regression: apps/api/test/automation-create-guard.int.test.ts (3 tests); fake game control.throwPendingActor (test/support/fake-automation.ts).
     Pre-fix check: with the create path temporarily reverted to the old code -> 2 of 3 tests failed (create answered 500); restored -> 3/3 passed:
       vitest run test/automation-create-guard.int.test.ts (old create path) -> 'Tests 2 failed | 1 passed (3)'
       vitest run test/automation-create-guard.int.test.ts (fixed)           -> 'Tests 3 passed (3)'
F-2  packages/games/rebellion/test/rules/core/hidden-info.test.ts (TC-H-02 seeded games x3) and invariants.test.ts (x3):
     explicit per-test timeout 30 000 ms via vitest options ({ timeout }), same seeds/steps/assertions (no coverage change).
F-5  openai-commander.strategy.ts: onUnexpectedError(errorName, sessionId); automation.providers.ts logs sessionId of the run
     (gameId/step unknown to the strategy -> masked '?'/0). AiUsage.budgetKey already = sessionId (unchanged).
     Test: test/automation/openai-commander-strategy.unit.test.ts (Q-20 expects the session id; new 'review F-5' test on createCommanderStrategy line).
F-8  packages/games/rebellion/src/ai/describe.ts: '(bot difficulty X)' -> '(game difficulty setting: X)'; test/ai/describe.test.ts updated
     (+ not.toContain('bot difficulty')). No snapshots/fixtures contained the phrase; W8 sim fixtures and prompt-invariance tests pass (see suites).

